			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement debug session tracking and DAP adapter spawning\n\nAdd DebugSessionEntry struct and DebugSessions map to DebugState for lifecycle management of active debug sessions. Implement StartDebugging to spawn executable adapters (node, chrome, etc.) with stdin/stdout/stderr pipes, parse DAP frames from adapter stdout, and emit messages on `sky://debug/dap-message`. Implement SendCommand to route DAP requests to the spawned adapter's stdin or fall back to reverse-RPC for inline-implementation adapters. Implement StopDebugging to send DAP disconnect and unregister the session.\n\nAlso implement OnSaveCustomDocument in CustomEditorProvider to reverse-RPC to the extension sidecar via `$onSaveCustomDocument`, replacing the stub.\n\nFix char-aware truncation in WindServiceHandlers and OutputChannelAppend to avoid panics when slicing multi-byte UTF-8 codepoints (e.g., `•` in SCM progress messages).",
			"SHA": "0b6ac619c4e7e5af9b04d1cd45731dbdd4959176"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T15:54:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Fix workspace boot seeding from recently-opened list and SCM handle alignment\n\nTwo issues addressed in this commit:\n\n1. **Recently-opened workspace fallback (CliParse.rs)**\n   The webview's initial URL is built from `~/.land/workspaces/RecentlyOpened.json`'s top entry (see `Binary/Build/WindowBuild.rs::BuildInitialUrl`), but Mountain's boot-time seeder previously fell straight through to CWD walk-up. This caused a mismatch: webview title said \"Mountain\" while Cocoon's init payload shipped \"Land\", vscode.git scanned the wrong root, and the SCM panel reported zeros despite uncommitted changes in the actual folder.\n\n   Add a fallback that probes the same source of truth as `BuildInitialUrl`, slotting it between env/CLI (explicit user intent) and CWD walk-up (last resort).\n\n2. **SCM provider handle alignment (3 files)**\n   Mountain was allocating new handles via DJB hash while Cocoon uses sequential handles from `ScmNamespace.ts`. When `UpdateSourceControlGroup` arrived with Cocoon's sequential handle, the lookup in Mountain's marker map failed because it was keyed by the hash instead.\n\n   - Honor caller-supplied `Handle` in `CreateSourceControl` (SourceControlManagementProvider.rs)\n   - Pass the same `Handle` through to `CreateData` in RPC/CocoonService/SCM.rs\n   - Include `handle` on the wire in Vine notification (RegisterScmProvider.rs)\n\nThis ensures all three components key their marker maps under the same identifier, allowing group updates to reach the SCM viewlet correctly.",
			"SHA": "c6897f8464e700b43fbece81e2be179d6e418623"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T15:18:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				2
			],
			"Message": "Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Mountain into Current",
			"SHA": "dcaa4d503dd7943dcba75ba06c867c9da7377a2d"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T14:48:29Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				859,
				21
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Align event payloads to Sky listener wire shapes and fix silent event drops\n\nThis commit addresses multiple issues where Mountain was emitting events that never reached Sky because of mismatched channel names or payload keys.\n\n**Event Channel Corrections (5 files)**\n- Terminal: `sky://terminal/opened` → `sky://terminal/create`, `sky://terminal/closed` → `sky://terminal/exit` (Sky listens on the new names at SkyBridge.ts:1736,1752)\n- Debug: `sky://debug/stop` → `sky://debug/sessionEnd` (SkyBridge.ts:2234)\n- StatusBar: `sky://statusbar/create` → `sky://statusbar/set-entry` (SkyBridge.ts:744 has no create listener)\n- Webview message: `sky://webview/message` → `sky://webview/post-message` (matches SkyBridge.ts:2344)\n- Progress: `sky://progress/report` → `sky://notification/progress-update` (aligns with notification namespace)\n\n**Payload Key Casing (8 files)**\n- OutputProvider: PascalCase keys (`Id`, `AppendedText`, `Name`, `LanguageId`) → camelCase (`channel`, `text`, `name`, `languageId`)\n- StatusBarProvider: Align all keys to camelCase\n- TreeViewProvider: `ViewIdentifier` → `viewId`, `ElementHandle` → `elementHandle`, `IsExpanded` → `expanded`\n- UserInterfaceProvider: `Severity`, `Message`, `Items` → `severity`, `message`, `items`\n- Window: `panelId` key alignment\n\n**Parameter Key Fallback (4 files)**\n- RegisterCommand/Provider: Probe camelCase first (`languageSelector`, `extensionId`) then snake_case for transitional compatibility\n- RegisterScmProvider/ResourceGroup: Probe camelCase (`scmHandle`, `rootUri`) then legacy snake_case\n\n**SCM RootUri Fix (RegisterScmProvider.rs)**\n- Previous extraction read only `path` component from UriComponents, producing relative URLs that failed to parse\n- Now reconstructs full `<scheme>://<authority><path>` triple from scheme/authority/path/query/fragment components\n- Falls back to `file://` prefix for bare paths, never emits relative URLs\n\n**Command Registry Sync (RegisterCommand.rs, UnregisterCommand.rs)**\n- Add emissions to `sky://command/register` and `sky://command/unregister` so Sky's workbench command palette sees extension-contributed commands\n\nWithout these fixes, terminal panes, tree views, status bar entries, and command palette entries were silently failing to render despite Mountain processing the underlying requests.",
			"SHA": "ba479c6a5ea13640cdd3164452f55f429472915f"
		},
